214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (ABOVE: Simplified screen shot \(excludes direct sponsor purchases\) of team books showing income and expenses of the team through the 2025-2026 season.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (Financial planning of the team is primarily done through our team captains and with the guidance of our coaches and mentors. The funds of our team are held by the finance department of the school; and as a result we are responsible for accounting, as well as up-keeping and maintaining accurate books. Our team sets up budgets to maintain incoming and outgoing funds. This allows us to plan changes in robot design as well as the cost of upcoming events and team plans.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (By up-keeping our accounting books, we are able to track not only our current financial standing but also the predicted funds that we need in the future. In addition, our financial plan allows us to budget before jumping into new robot builds. We are also able to account for future needs such as next year's registration and the funds that will be needed as we advance through the current season.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (Additionally, these financial books allow us to account for the amount we need to fundraise. A great example of this is the expenses we had at last season's state championship. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (In financing our robot and our season, the majority of our funds comes from sponsorships, grants secured from local businesses and companies in our area. Running the program primarily off of sponsor donations places the importance into two areas: securing new sponsors and retaining relationships with current sponsors.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (Since it was our first time going, we did not know the full scope of the event. We had only accounted for expenses for further robot design, food, and lodging. It was not until we got to the championship that we understood how big the pit environment and culture was. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (Moving into this season, we now have allocated additional funds into our budget in hopes that if we are able to attend this season that we can participate in all aspects of the state championship to our highest ability.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (In securing a new sponsor, we use a sponsorship form. This form allows us to articulate the levels of sponsorship as well as what we offer to our sponsors at different levels. We primarily reach out to potential sponsors in the off-season. To do this, we either go to the location in person or send an email an executive. Typically, we check back in with the business after two weeks.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 77 0 R
/A [654 0 R 0]
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (ABOVE: Simplified screen shot of teams sponsorship form showing the different levels and offers for each level.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (We find that maintaining sponsor relationships is just as important as finding them. Initially when the team started we)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (found that if the sponsor was not updated on the team and our success, they would be less likely to join us for the following season. Knowing this, we try to update our sponsors monthly with newsletters and social media shoutouts. At the end of the season, we take the time to formally thank our sponsors. We update them on the results of the season, and how their contribution helped make it happen.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
