<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Learning from our experience at the state championship last season, we decided to view robot iterations and improvements differently. In previous seasons, we opted for full bot redesigns between competitions. This design process made us feel like we were always trying to catch up to the competition. Coming into this season, we looked at iterations as fine tuning changes to individual systems. In doing this we were also able to preserve our base code in addition to the fluidity between system transfers.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (To ensure we use our time efficiently, we now follow a set design process. When deciding on a potential design change, we first render a functioning model in CAD. After the CAD model is complete, we begin building physical prototypes. Once there is a functional and heavily tested prototype, we implement the change to our robot.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
