274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (Coming into this season, we aim to have our strategy revolve around the motif points. We felt that the best way to do this would be to allow the bot to pick up and choose which artifact we wanted before launching. Solidifying this strategy, we added a horizontal spinning indexer to our design that we kept through the whole season. As we moved through the season, some changes to the indexer were made to optimize the design.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (For Meet 3, we continued to face jamming issues. In addition, we realized the slower speed of the indexer was hurting our cycle time. To resolve this, we removed the slotted walls and instead added built-in indexer walls with much more height and width to fully encompass the artifacts. These changes allowed for the artifacts to be transferred at much higher speeds without getting jammed.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (Our first design of the indexer was a mix between a fidget spinner and a spinning plate. To allow for better control over the artifacts, indentations were added in addition to interchangeable divider walls. This allowed for the artifacts to stay stationary and minimized the risk of them falling out, or rolling into another slot.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (As we moved to using a magnetic limit switch for calibration, a receded hole for a magnet was added to the underside of the indexer.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (ABOVE: The first iteration of the indexer was a simple rotating plate with indentions for the balls to sit as they rotated.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (In Meet 2, we faced jamming issues caused by interference with the artifacts against the portion holding the axle and motor for the indexer. We also faced artifact detection issues because of the holes on the artifact. Our solution to these issues was to implement bigger walls which flared out to better contain the artifacts in their respected areas. In addition, we made the outer walls curve around the indexer to prevent the artifacts from getting loose. We changed the positioning of the color sensors to have more surface area to read the artifacts in which helped with the detection issues.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
