287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (This solved the majority of the problem, but this solution was still rather slow and inaccurate. To solve this, we had to take a new approach. We changed the mounting position of the kicker from the bottom to the top of the robot. We also extended the arm of the transfer mechanism. This solution works faster than the previous version as the paddle for the arm is much farther away than the source of rotation causing faster relative motion. Another change we made to the transfer system was to cup the end of the arm. On top of this, a limit switch was added in this phase to detect when retraction of the kicker was complete so we can start rotating immediately. This design works much more reliably to guide the artifact in and is a much intuitive solution to the transfer issue.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (The transfer system, or kicker, started out being mounted below the indexer. The first iteration of the transfer system rotated through premade cutouts on the indexer tray, to push the artifacts into the shooting mechanism. There were slight issues with the first iteration however; the kicker was too short to successfully push the artifacts into the shooter and as such was commonly inaccurate. To fix this problem, we revamped the indexer to have larger holes in the trays so that the transfer mechanism arm can be longer.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
