294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (The shooter system consists of two fly wheels arranged horizontally that grip onto the artifact and launch it into the goal. In the first iteration, we had it so the shooter could tilt forward and back via 2 servos on either side of the shoot. We found that this caused variability and slowed cycle time because of constantly having to readjust; so we changed it to be static in the rest of our iterations.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (In our first static design, we added a wedge at the bottom of the shooter to increase our launch angle. This addition also induced spin onto the ball. To allow for the ball to shoot in an arc, we raised the top part of our shooter to be arched.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (We ended up finding variability in the path that the artifact took inside of the shooter prior to interacting with the fly wheels. To fix this, our last iteration incorporated a chute that fit the around the artifact. Additionally, we swapped the ramp for a rubber bumper to better induce spin onto the ball.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (As we approach league championships, we plan on imparting 2 more changes to our shooter. Firstly, we plan on reducing the amount of compression we have on the artifact by increasing the space between our two fly wheels. After that, we would like to increase the amount of friction on the artifact through the shooter to further increase spin and therefore accuracy in our artifacts flight path.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
