306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (We added quality of life features to help the drivers and the coders with completing their tasks more efficiently. One example would be our toggle features on the controllers to make robot slower for the drivers. With this, we can park and aim with more accuracy. This also allows us to drive more carefully around protected zones.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (We made most of our systems automatic so we could save time during matches. For example, our indexer turns automatically when the front color sensor detects an artifact. In addition, our transfer system has a limit switch that notifies us when the indexer is safe to move again. This avoids the problem of the indexer accidentally colliding with the transfer mechanism.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (When it comes to coding, accessibility is key. When we make code, we always make sure to add documentation comments to help other programmers understand what specific parts of code are used for. We also make sure to review code for code smells, depriving the code of any unnecessary methods, classes, or counter-intuitive code. This makes reading the code simpler for others to review. We also made documents to each component's configuration in the Control Hub. This way engineers can replug components if any changes are made.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
