365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (There were multiple issues we were able to solve with sensors. Originally, there was only one color sensor reviewing our indexer. To account for errors, now we have three. Additionally, the color sensors on the robot also act as distance sensors. When an artifact gets seen, the indexer knows that it is ready to move on. However, if the color of the artifact is not able to be read in time, the other color sensors would be able to correct it. To counter misalignment, we installed a magnet onto the indexer, and a magnet sensor underneath the indexer. When aligned with the magnet sensor, we know that its positioning is correct and that we are realigned.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
